    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-03-09T08:54:42Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nAlthough a neat idea, I don't think this will happen in 'mini.pairs'. Its main purpose is to be as simple and fast as possible. Having to check for tree-sitter context each time a pair character is typed (which is quite frequent), goes against this design decision.\r\n\r\nRight now there is an only mechanism to decide whether a typed character needs special treatment, and that is [`neigh_pattern`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3b37f4afb933141a750b60b86fb6ef6b50d0e61/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L137-L139). For single quote it already is by default [such that only single one is inserted after a Latin letter](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3b37f4afb933141a750b60b86fb6ef6b50d0e61/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L121). This looks like a more reasonable compromise for this problem.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Although a neat idea, I don't think this will happen in 'mini.pairs'. Its main purpose is to be as simple and fast as possible. Having to check for tree-sitter context each time a pair character is typed (which is quite frequent), goes against this design decision.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Right now there is an only mechanism to decide whether a typed character needs special treatment, and that is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3b37f4afb933141a750b60b86fb6ef6b50d0e61/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L137-L139\"><code class=\"notranslate\">neigh_pattern</code></a>. For single quote it already is by default <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3b37f4afb933141a750b60b86fb6ef6b50d0e61/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L121\">such that only single one is inserted after a Latin letter</a>. This looks like a more reasonable compromise for this problem.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for the suggestion!\nAlthough a neat idea, I don't think this will happen in 'mini.pairs'. Its main purpose is to be as simple and fast as possible. Having to check for tree-sitter context each time a pair character is typed (which is quite frequent), goes against this design decision.\nRight now there is an only mechanism to decide whether a typed character needs special treatment, and that is neigh_pattern. For single quote it already is by default such that only single one is inserted after a Latin letter. This looks like a more reasonable compromise for this problem.",
