                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "@echasnovski I understand!\r\n\r\nI feel like there are a lot of situation where a pair char shouldn't be doubled.\r\nFor example in Rust, when using lifetimes, the single quote is used a lot!\r\nEg:\r\n```rust\r\nimpl<'a> WatchablePath<'a> {\r\n    pub fn recursive(path: &'a Path) -> Self {\r\n        Self {\r\n            path,\r\n            mode: RecursiveMode::Recursive,\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI feel like tree-sitter would be a more robust solution than modifying the neigh_pattern for single quotes?",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> I understand!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I feel like there are a lot of situation where a pair char shouldn't be doubled.<br>\nFor example in Rust, when using lifetimes, the single quote is used a lot!<br>\nEg:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"impl&lt;'a&gt; WatchablePath&lt;'a&gt; {\n    pub fn recursive(path: &amp;'a Path) -&gt; Self {\n        Self {\n            path,\n            mode: RecursiveMode::Recursive,\n        }\n    }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">impl</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">'</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">a</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">WatchablePath</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">'</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">a</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">pub</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">recursive</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">path</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">'</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">a</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">Path</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> -&gt; <span class=\"pl-smi\">Self</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">Self</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n            path<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"pl-c1\">mode</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">RecursiveMode</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span><span class=\"pl-v\">Recursive</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I feel like tree-sitter would be a more robust solution than modifying the neigh_pattern for single quotes?</p>",
                    "bodyText": "@echasnovski I understand!\nI feel like there are a lot of situation where a pair char shouldn't be doubled.\nFor example in Rust, when using lifetimes, the single quote is used a lot!\nEg:\nimpl<'a> WatchablePath<'a> {\n    pub fn recursive(path: &'a Path) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            path,\n            mode: RecursiveMode::Recursive,\n        }\n    }\n}\nI feel like tree-sitter would be a more robust solution than modifying the neigh_pattern for single quotes?",
