                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> For example in Rust, when using lifetimes, the single quote is used a lot!\r\n\r\nThen my suggestion would be to disable single quote pair for `rust` filetype.\r\n\r\n> I feel like tree-sitter would be a more robust solution than modifying the neigh_pattern for single quotes?\r\n\r\nProbably yes, but at the cost of significantly more computations done quite frequently. Which feels like a too big price to pay for this.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example in Rust, when using lifetimes, the single quote is used a lot!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Then my suggestion would be to disable single quote pair for <code class=\"notranslate\">rust</code> filetype.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I feel like tree-sitter would be a more robust solution than modifying the neigh_pattern for single quotes?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Probably yes, but at the cost of significantly more computations done quite frequently. Which feels like a too big price to pay for this.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "For example in Rust, when using lifetimes, the single quote is used a lot!\n\nThen my suggestion would be to disable single quote pair for rust filetype.\n\nI feel like tree-sitter would be a more robust solution than modifying the neigh_pattern for single quotes?\n\nProbably yes, but at the cost of significantly more computations done quite frequently. Which feels like a too big price to pay for this.",
